<title>USA: Lexington IPO raises number of shares.</title>
<headline>Lexington IPO raises number of shares.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The proposed number of shares for the planned initial public offering in Lexington Healthcare Group Inc has been raised to 1.125 million shares from one million shares originally, lead underwriter Mason Hill &amp; Co Inc said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The estimated target price for the planned initial public offering will remain $5 per share.  Lexington Healthcare Group, a longterm and subacute care provider, is expected to trade on Monday under the proposed symbol on the Nasdaq National Market.</p>
</text>
